IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `voca-schedules`
IMPORT `voca-core`
IMPORT `voca-seat`

-- Cases for the victim's seat (voca-seat.l4), the tables (voca-schedules.l4) and the regulative rules of the core
-- (voca-core.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited Act (REPV014) and Regulations (REPV014R1),
-- never copied from the encoding's output; the arithmetic is in the comment above each assertion. No scenario life
-- covers the Northern Territory, so every person here is HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- A breached or still-pending DEONTIC cannot be asserted on the stable l4, so regulative rules are asserted where the
-- trace ends FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line where it does not. Clock: days.
--
-- Argument order of the two act questions (16 answers): in the NT; a criminal offence or excused; directly caused
-- injury or death; Criminal Code section; attempt; date of the offence; serious harm; offensive weapon; in company;
-- old s 188(2)(a), (c), (k); the Schedule 2 condition; number of related acts; over a period of time; same offender and
-- victim.

`1 Jul 2025`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2025
`1 Jun 2022`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2022
`1 Jun 2023`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2023
`1 Jan 2020`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020
`1 Jan 2024`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2024

-- One injury, not scarring (or permanent scarring not from burns).
GIVEN `item`       IS A STRING
      `both sides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `existing`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `My injury`
`injury` `item` `both sides` `existing` MEANS
    `My injury` WITH
        `its Schedule 3 item`                                    IS `item`
        `it is on both sides of my body, or to my only remaining one` IS `both sides`
        `the percent the assessor puts down to a condition I already had` IS `existing`
        `for scarring, it is permanent`                          IS TRUE
        `for scarring, it was caused by burns I also claim for that part` IS FALSE

-- A scarring injury.
GIVEN `item`      IS A STRING
      `permanent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `burns`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My injury`
`scar` `item` `permanent` `burns` MEANS
    `My injury` WITH
        `its Schedule 3 item`                                    IS `item`
        `it is on both sides of my body, or to my only remaining one` IS FALSE
        `the percent the assessor puts down to a condition I already had` IS 0
        `for scarring, it is permanent`                          IS `permanent`
        `for scarring, it was caused by burns I also claim for that part` IS `burns`

GIVEN `c` IS A BOOLEAN
      `i` IS A BOOLEAN
      `l` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a` IS A BOOLEAN
      `j` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What may be applied for`
`may` `c` `i` `l` `a` `j` MEANS
    `What may be applied for` WITH
        `counselling`                                              IS `c`
        `an interim payment for financial loss`                    IS `i`
        `an award for financial loss`                              IS `l`
        `an award for the mere commission of a compensable violent act` IS `a`
        `an award for compensable injuries`                        IS `j`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 1. The violent act and its category (s 5, s 7(1), regs 4, 6, 7, 14, Schedule 1). HYPOTHETICAL offences in
-- Darwin; dates as given.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 208H (current Code), no aggravation, one act, no injury: a Schedule 1 offence, so a violent act under s 5(1)(a)
-- without any injury. Schedule 1, Part 2 row "An offence against section 208H or 208HA" (no qualification): category 2,
-- Part 5(b) $20 000.
#ASSERT `Is it a violent act` TRUE TRUE FALSE "208H" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE FALSE "208H" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 2 20000
-- With an offensive weapon (one factor of aggravation, reg 7(b)): Part 3 row "208H ... If a factor of aggravation
-- applies": category 3, $30 000.
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE FALSE "208H" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 3 30000
-- With a weapon and in company (two factors): Part 4 "An offence mentioned in Part 3 -- If at least 2 factors of
-- aggravation apply": category 4, $40 000.
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE FALSE "208H" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 4 40000
-- An attempt at s 208H, no aggravation: Part 1 row "An offence of attempting to commit an offence against section 208H
-- or 208HA": category 1, $10 000 (finding 7: the attempt is a lower category despite s 5(7)).
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE FALSE "208H" TRUE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 1 10000
-- An attempt with serious harm: Part 1 (attempt, none) and Part 2 (attempt, if a factor applies): highest, category 2.
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE TRUE "208H" TRUE `1 Jul 2025` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 2 20000
-- s 208AB: Part 1 without qualification; with serious harm also Part 2 ("If a factor of aggravation applies"). READING:
-- the highest Part, category 2 (finding 6). Without aggravation, category 1.
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE TRUE "208AB" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 2 20000
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE FALSE "208AB" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 1 10000
-- s 208J as a pattern of abuse: 4 related acts over a period of time by the same offender against the same victim
-- (reg 6). Part 2 names s 208J; Part 4 "An offence mentioned in Part 1, 2 or 3 ... must involve a pattern of abuse":
-- category 4. The same four acts at about the same time are no pattern: Part 2, category 2.
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE FALSE "208J" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 4 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 4 40000
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE FALSE "208J" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 4 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 2 20000
-- s 208JI: Part 4 by name, category 4.
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE FALSE "208JI" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 4 40000
-- Old s 192(3), committed 1 June 2022 (before 25 March 2024): Part 2 "Criminal Code as in force before ..." row "An
-- offence against section 192(3)": category 2.
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE FALSE "192(3)" FALSE `1 Jun 2022` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 2 20000
-- The same section number for an act on 1 July 2025: the old heading does not apply, so not in Schedule 1; with an
-- injury it is still a violent act under s 5(1)(b).
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE TRUE "192(3)" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not a compensable violent act: the offence is not in Schedule 1 (s 7(1), reg 4)`
#ASSERT `Is it a violent act` TRUE TRUE TRUE "192(3)" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Old s 188 on 1 June 2023 with s 188(2)(a), (c) and (k): Part 1, category 1. With (a) and (c) only: not in Schedule 1.
-- With all three and an offensive weapon: also Part 2 ("those circumstances ... and a factor of aggravation"): 2.
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE TRUE "188" FALSE `1 Jun 2023` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 1 10000
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE TRUE "188" FALSE `1 Jun 2023` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not a compensable violent act: the offence is not in Schedule 1 (s 7(1), reg 4)`
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE TRUE "188" FALSE `1 Jun 2023` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 2 20000
-- A common assault under the current s 188 that injures: a violent act (s 5(1)(b)), not a compensable one.
#ASSERT `Is it a violent act` TRUE TRUE TRUE "188" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE TRUE "188" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not a compensable violent act: the offence is not in Schedule 1 (s 7(1), reg 4)`
-- The same assault in Queensland: not a violent act (s 5(1)(b)(i): "occurs in the Territory").
#ASSERT `Is it a violent act` FALSE TRUE TRUE "188" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` FALSE TRUE TRUE "208H" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not a violent act (s 5)`
-- An accident that is no offence at all: not a violent act. One that would be an offence but for the offender's age
-- (s 5(2)(b)): a violent act.
#ASSERT `Is it a violent act` TRUE FALSE TRUE "" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is it a violent act` TRUE TRUE TRUE "" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Old s 131A on 1 January 2020: Part 4 "Criminal Code as in force before ..." row: category 4.
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE FALSE "131A" FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 4 40000
-- s 186B: completed, Part 3 (category 3); attempted, Part 2 (category 2); completed with two factors, Part 4.
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE FALSE "186B" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 3 30000
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE FALSE "186B" TRUE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 2 20000
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE TRUE "186B" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 4 40000
-- s 125D: none, Part 2 (2); one factor, Part 3 (3); two factors, Part 4 (4).
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE FALSE "125D" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 2 20000
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE FALSE "125D" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 3 30000
#ASSERT `What category of compensable violent act is it` TRUE TRUE TRUE "125D" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a compensable violent act` 4 40000

-- Schedule 2 (reg 15): which offences can found a category 1 or 2 disorder. Offence answers in the order of
-- `the offence from my answers` (13).
-- s 156 (murder): listed. s 196 only "If committed ... on the person's unlawful entry of a building".
#ASSERT `the offence is specified in Schedule 1 or 2` (`the offence from my answers` "156" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the offence is specified in Schedule 1 or 2` (`the offence from my answers` "196" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the offence is specified in Schedule 1 or 2` (`the offence from my answers` "196" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 1 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
-- Old s 211(1) in its s 211(2) circumstance: listed for an offence before 30 April 2023 only.
#ASSERT `the offence is specified in Schedule 1 or 2` (`the offence from my answers` "211(1)" FALSE `1 Jun 2022` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 1 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the offence is specified in Schedule 1 or 2` (`the offence from my answers` "211(1)" FALSE `1 Jan 2024` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 1 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
-- A current common assault (s 188): in neither Schedule (finding 17). Old s 188 with (c) and (k): Schedule 2, though
-- not Schedule 1, which needs (a) as well.
#ASSERT `the offence is specified in Schedule 1 or 2` (`the offence from my answers` "188" FALSE `1 Jul 2025` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the offence is specified in Schedule 1 or 2` (`the offence from my answers` "188" FALSE `1 Jun 2023` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
-- An attempt at s 156: Schedule 2 lists completed offences only (reg 7A).
#ASSERT `the offence is specified in Schedule 1 or 2` (`the offence from my answers` "156" TRUE `1 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 2. Injury (s 6), domestic violence injuries (reg 5) and the psychological disorder item (reg 15, item 12).
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 6(1)(a)-(c), (2).
#ASSERT `Is my harm an injury` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my harm an injury` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my harm an injury` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my harm an injury` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my harm an injury` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- reg 5: a pattern of abuse by a domestic partner, injuries more than trifling: yes. Trifling: no. Stalking in breach
-- of a DVO: yes. No injury: no. An injury from an act that is neither: no.
#ASSERT `Did I suffer domestic violence injuries` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Did I suffer domestic violence injuries` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Did I suffer domestic violence injuries` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Did I suffer domestic violence injuries` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Did I suffer domestic violence injuries` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- reg 15 and item 12. Severely disabling, chronic, from a listed offence, 60 weeks: category 2, "more than 52 weeks":
-- 12(b)(ii). Moderately, chronic, listed offence, 20 weeks: 12(a)(i).
#ASSERT `Which Schedule 3 item is my disorder` `severely disabling` TRUE TRUE FALSE 60 FALSE EQUALS `my disorder is Schedule 3 item` "12(b)(ii)"
#ASSERT `Which Schedule 3 item is my disorder` `moderately disabling` TRUE TRUE FALSE 20 FALSE EQUALS `my disorder is Schedule 3 item` "12(a)(i)"
-- Moderately disabling, from domestic violence injuries but no listed offence: category 1 needs a listed offence, so
-- no item (finding 17). Severely disabling from domestic violence injuries, 30 weeks: 12(b)(i).
#ASSERT `Which Schedule 3 item is my disorder` `moderately disabling` TRUE FALSE TRUE 60 FALSE EQUALS `my disorder has no Schedule 3 item 12 amount (reg 15: it must be chronic, at least moderately disabling, from a Schedule 1 or 2 offence or, if severely disabling, from domestic violence injuries, and last more than 13 weeks)`
#ASSERT `Which Schedule 3 item is my disorder` `severely disabling` TRUE FALSE TRUE 30 FALSE EQUALS `my disorder is Schedule 3 item` "12(b)(i)"
-- 10 weeks: item 12 starts at "more than 13 weeks". Not chronic: neither category. Permanent: (ii).
#ASSERT `Which Schedule 3 item is my disorder` `severely disabling` TRUE TRUE FALSE 10 FALSE EQUALS `my disorder has no Schedule 3 item 12 amount (reg 15: it must be chronic, at least moderately disabling, from a Schedule 1 or 2 offence or, if severely disabling, from domestic violence injuries, and last more than 13 weeks)`
#ASSERT `Which Schedule 3 item is my disorder` `moderately disabling` FALSE TRUE FALSE 60 FALSE EQUALS `my disorder has no Schedule 3 item 12 amount (reg 15: it must be chronic, at least moderately disabling, from a Schedule 1 or 2 offence or, if severely disabling, from domestic violence injuries, and last more than 13 weeks)`
#ASSERT `Which Schedule 3 item is my disorder` `moderately disabling` TRUE TRUE FALSE 5 TRUE EQUALS `my disorder is Schedule 3 item` "12(a)(ii)"

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 3. What kind of victim (ss 9, 11, 13, 15). Answers in order: violent act; compensable; against me; injured;
-- injured as rescuer; present and injured by witnessing; injured on learning later; child of the primary victim;
-- parent of the primary victim; primary victim a child; spouse; dependent; relative or intimate; committed it.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Ben, assaulted and injured: primary (s 9(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `Which kinds of victim am I` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `primary victim`
-- A compensable violent act against Aroha, no injury: still primary (s 9(1)(a)). The same without a compensable act:
-- no category.
#ASSERT `Which kinds of victim am I` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `primary victim`
#ASSERT `Which kinds of victim am I` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (EMPTY)
-- A passer-by injured trying to stop it: primary (s 9(2)).
#ASSERT `Which kinds of victim am I` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `primary victim`
-- The mother of a child victim, present and injured by witnessing: secondary (s 11(1)) and family (s 13(1)(b)); she
-- applies in one only (s 25(1)).
#ASSERT `Which kinds of victim am I` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS LIST `secondary victim`, `family victim`
-- A spouse, not injured: family. A brother, not injured: related (not family, s 15(2)(a)). A brother who witnessed it
-- and was injured: secondary and related.
#ASSERT `Which kinds of victim am I` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS LIST `family victim`
#ASSERT `Which kinds of victim am I` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS LIST `related victim`
#ASSERT `Which kinds of victim am I` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS LIST `secondary victim`, `related victim`
-- A spouse who committed the act: none of the categories (ss 11(3), 13(4), 15(2)(b)).
#ASSERT `Which kinds of victim am I` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (EMPTY)
-- The parent of an adult victim, injured on learning of it later: s 11(2)(b) needs a child primary victim, so family
-- only. The child of a primary victim, injured on learning of it: secondary (s 11(2)(a)) and family.
#ASSERT `Which kinds of victim am I` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS LIST `family victim`
#ASSERT `Which kinds of victim am I` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS LIST `secondary victim`, `family victim`
-- Not a violent act: no category, even for a spouse. A dependent housemate who is no relative: family (s 13(1)(d)).
#ASSERT `Which kinds of victim am I` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (EMPTY)
#ASSERT `Which kinds of victim am I` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `family victim`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 4. What may I apply for (ss 10, 12, 14, 16, 17, 18, 22, 25, 26). Answers in order: category; compensable act;
-- compensable injury; hardship; primary victim died; MAC paid; MAC entitled; worker; RTW paid; RTW entitled; RTW
-- disputed; already applied for an award; award decided; interim already paid. Expected in the order counselling,
-- interim, award for loss, award for the act, award for injuries.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Aroha, primary victim of a compensable act with a compensable injury, in hardship: everything (s 10).
#ASSERT `What may I apply for` `primary victim` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `may` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- A related victim: counselling only (s 16).
#ASSERT `What may I apply for` `related victim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `may` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A family victim of a homicide, not in hardship: counselling and an award for financial loss (s 14(1), (3)).
#ASSERT `What may I apply for` `family victim` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `may` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- A family victim where the primary victim survived: counselling only, even in hardship (s 14(2)-(3) need the death).
#ASSERT `What may I apply for` `family victim` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `may` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A worker assaulted at work and being paid Return to Work compensation: counselling only (s 18(1), (4)).
#ASSERT `What may I apply for` `primary victim` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `may` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Interim payments already at $5 000: no further interim payment (s 25(3)); the rest stays open.
#ASSERT `What may I apply for` `primary victim` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 5000 EQUALS `may` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- A secondary victim with a compensable injury, in hardship: no award for the act (s 12 has none).
#ASSERT `What may I apply for` `secondary victim` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `may` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- A primary victim whose award application is in and decided: no interim (s 26(2A)), no second award (s 25(2)).
#ASSERT `What may I apply for` `primary victim` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 EQUALS `may` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A secondary victim of an act against someone entitled to a MAC benefit: counselling only (s 17(3), (4)(b)).
#ASSERT `What may I apply for` `secondary victim` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `may` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A worker whose Return to Work claim is disputed and undecided: presumed not entitled (reg 13(2)), so not excluded.
#ASSERT `What may I apply for` `primary victim` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `may` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 5. Injured at work or on the road (ss 17, 18, reg 13). Answers: injured person; MAC paid; MAC entitled; worker;
-- RTW paid; RTW entitled; RTW disputed.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Carlos, hit by a car driven at him deliberately: entitled to a MAC benefit, never claimed: excluded (s 17(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `Does another scheme stop my claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `excluded as the injured person, for that injury: a Motor Accidents (Compensation) benefit is paid or payable (s 17(1)); counselling stays open`
-- His daughter, who saw it: excluded as a secondary victim (s 17(3)).
#ASSERT `Does another scheme stop my claim` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `excluded as a secondary or family victim: the injured person is covered by the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act (s 17(3)); counselling stays open`
-- Dana, a nurse assaulted at work; her claim is disputed and in mediation: not excluded for now (reg 13(2)).
#ASSERT `Does another scheme stop my claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not excluded for now: a disputed Return to Work claim is presumed not to be an entitlement (reg 13(2)); the assessor may defer in exceptional circumstances (reg 13(3))`
-- If she has been paid compensation (provisional payments) the presumption does not help: s 18(1)(a).
#ASSERT `Does another scheme stop my claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `excluded as the injured person, for that injury: Return to Work compensation is paid or payable (s 18(1)); counselling stays open`
-- Entitled, but never claimed: excluded (s 18(1)(b), "regardless of whether the worker has made a claim"; finding 9).
#ASSERT `Does another scheme stop my claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `excluded as the injured person, for that injury: Return to Work compensation is paid or payable (s 18(1)); counselling stays open`
-- Not a worker under the Return to Work Act: s 18 cannot apply. Nothing at all: not excluded.
#ASSERT `Does another scheme stop my claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not excluded by s 17 or s 18`
#ASSERT `Does another scheme stop my claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not excluded by s 17 or s 18`
-- Dana's partner, a family victim, if she is entitled: excluded (s 18(3)).
#ASSERT `Does another scheme stop my claim` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `excluded as a secondary or family victim: the injured worker is covered by the Return to Work Act (s 18(3)); counselling stays open`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 6. Interim payment (ss 25(3), 26(2A), 27(5)). Answers: category; hardship; primary victim died; excluded; award
-- decided; interim already had; the loss.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Ben, in hardship, $7 000 of loss, nothing paid yet: up to $5 000 (s 27(5)).
#ASSERT `How much interim payment can I apply for` `primary victim` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 7000 EQUALS `I may apply for an interim payment of up to` 5000
-- A second interim payment after $3 000, for $3 000 more loss: up to $2 000 (s 25(3)).
#ASSERT `How much interim payment can I apply for` `primary victim` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 3000 3000 EQUALS `I may apply for an interim payment of up to` 2000
-- A family victim of a homicide in hardship, $4 000 loss: $4 000.
#ASSERT `How much interim payment can I apply for` `family victim` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 4000 EQUALS `I may apply for an interim payment of up to` 4000
-- Cannot: family victim, no death; related victim; award decided; no hardship; $5 000 already; excluded secondary.
#ASSERT `How much interim payment can I apply for` `family victim` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 4000 EQUALS `I cannot apply for an interim payment now (ss 10(2), 12(2), 14(2), 16, 17, 18, 25(3), 26(2A))`
#ASSERT `How much interim payment can I apply for` `related victim` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 4000 EQUALS `I cannot apply for an interim payment now (ss 10(2), 12(2), 14(2), 16, 17, 18, 25(3), 26(2A))`
#ASSERT `How much interim payment can I apply for` `primary victim` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 4000 EQUALS `I cannot apply for an interim payment now (ss 10(2), 12(2), 14(2), 16, 17, 18, 25(3), 26(2A))`
#ASSERT `How much interim payment can I apply for` `primary victim` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 4000 EQUALS `I cannot apply for an interim payment now (ss 10(2), 12(2), 14(2), 16, 17, 18, 25(3), 26(2A))`
#ASSERT `How much interim payment can I apply for` `primary victim` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 5000 4000 EQUALS `I cannot apply for an interim payment now (ss 10(2), 12(2), 14(2), 16, 17, 18, 25(3), 26(2A))`
#ASSERT `How much interim payment can I apply for` `secondary victim` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 4000 EQUALS `I cannot apply for an interim payment now (ss 10(2), 12(2), 14(2), 16, 17, 18, 25(3), 26(2A))`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 7. Standard amounts for compensable injuries (regs 16, 18-22, Schedule 3).
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- A broken upper arm, 6.7(a): $10 000. Both arms: reg 16(3)(ab) names 6.7, so doubled, $20 000. A fractured hip
-- (6.6(b), $15 500) "on each side": 6.6 is not named, so not doubled.
#ASSERT `What is the standard amount for my injuries` (LIST (`injury` "6.7(a)" FALSE 0)) EQUALS `the standard amount that may be awarded for the injuries, in dollars, is` 10000
#ASSERT `What is the standard amount for my injuries` (LIST (`injury` "6.7(a)" TRUE 0)) EQUALS `the standard amount that may be awarded for the injuries, in dollars, is` 20000
#ASSERT `What is the standard amount for my injuries` (LIST (`injury` "6.6(b)" TRUE 0)) EQUALS `the standard amount that may be awarded for the injuries, in dollars, is` 15500
-- Four injuries: 6.7(a) $10 000, 5.4(a) $3 000, 6.6(c)(i) $3 000, 5.5(c) $4 000. Ranked 10 000, 4 000, 3 000, 3 000;
-- reg 18(1): 10 000 + 30% x 4 000 + 15% x 3 000 = 10 000 + 1 200 + 450 = 11 650; the fourth adds nothing (reg 18(3)).
#ASSERT `What is the standard amount for my injuries` (LIST (`injury` "6.7(a)" FALSE 0), (`injury` "5.4(a)" FALSE 0), (`injury` "6.6(c)(i)" FALSE 0), (`injury` "5.5(c)" FALSE 0)) EQUALS `the standard amount that may be awarded for the injuries, in dollars, is` 11650
-- The arm with 25% put down to an old injury (reg 19): 10 000 x 75% = 7 500; plus 30% x 4 000 = 1 200: 8 700.
#ASSERT `What is the standard amount for my injuries` (LIST (`injury` "6.7(a)" FALSE 25), (`injury` "5.5(c)" FALSE 0)) EQUALS `the standard amount that may be awarded for the injuries, in dollars, is` 8700
-- Order does not matter: teeth first, arm second, 10 000 + 1 200 = 11 200.
#ASSERT `What is the standard amount for my injuries` (LIST (`injury` "5.5(c)" FALSE 0), (`injury` "6.7(a)" FALSE 0)) EQUALS `the standard amount that may be awarded for the injuries, in dollars, is` 11200
-- A tie at the first amount (6.7(a) and 7.2(a), $10 000 each): the second is the other $10 000 one (reg 18(2)(b)(i)):
-- 10 000 + 3 000 = 13 000.
#ASSERT `What is the standard amount for my injuries` (LIST (`injury` "6.7(a)" FALSE 0), (`injury` "7.2(a)" FALSE 0)) EQUALS `the standard amount that may be awarded for the injuries, in dollars, is` 13000
-- Domestic violence injuries (item 4) with a facial fracture: READING, the $10 000 domestic violence amount alone
-- (regs 18(4), 22(1)).
#ASSERT `What is the standard amount for my injuries` (LIST (`injury` "4" FALSE 0), (`injury` "6.1(a)" FALSE 0)) EQUALS `the standard amount that may be awarded for the injuries, in dollars, is` 10000
-- Moderate scarring that is not permanent: nothing (reg 21(2)); with the arm, the arm alone.
#ASSERT `What is the standard amount for my injuries` (LIST (`scar` "13(b)" FALSE FALSE), (`injury` "6.7(a)" FALSE 0)) EQUALS `the standard amount that may be awarded for the injuries, in dollars, is` 10000
-- Facial burns 2(c) $16 000 and severe scarring of the face from those burns: not both (reg 21(3)): 16 000.
#ASSERT `What is the standard amount for my injuries` (LIST (`injury` "2(c)" FALSE 0), (`scar` "13(c)" TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS `the standard amount that may be awarded for the injuries, in dollars, is` 16000
-- Permanent moderate scarring not from burns: $7 500.
#ASSERT `What is the standard amount for my injuries` (LIST (`scar` "13(b)" TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS `the standard amount that may be awarded for the injuries, in dollars, is` 7500
-- An item that is not a leaf of the table: not covered (the applicant must name the most similar listed item).
#ASSERT `What is the standard amount for my injuries` (LIST (`injury` "6.7(z)" FALSE 0)) EQUALS `not covered: this item is not a leaf of Schedule 3, Part 2 (give the most similar listed item, reg 16(1)(b))` "6.7(z)"
-- Loss of both eyes, 5.2(f) on each side: double $40 000 = $80 000 (s 38(1) caps the award; see case 9). No injuries:
-- nothing.
#ASSERT `What is the standard amount for my injuries` (LIST (`injury` "5.2(f)" TRUE 0)) EQUALS `the standard amount that may be awarded for the injuries, in dollars, is` 80000
#ASSERT `What is the standard amount for my injuries` (EMPTY) EQUALS `the standard amount that may be awarded for the injuries, in dollars, is` 0

-- The $7 500 threshold (ss 38(3), 39(3)). A skull fracture not needing surgery (6.5(a), $5 000) and a deviated septum
-- (5.4(a), $3 000): READING, the standard amounts total 8 000, so the threshold is met (finding 4), although reg 18
-- allows only 5 000 + 30% x 3 000 = 5 900.
#ASSERT `Do my injuries reach the threshold` (LIST (`injury` "6.5(a)" FALSE 0), (`injury` "5.4(a)" FALSE 0)) EQUALS `yes: the standard amounts total at least $7 500` 8000
#ASSERT `What is the standard amount for my injuries` (LIST (`injury` "6.5(a)" FALSE 0), (`injury` "5.4(a)" FALSE 0)) EQUALS `the standard amount that may be awarded for the injuries, in dollars, is` 5900
-- One lower-leg fracture (6.4(a)(i), $8 000): met. Loss of up to 3 teeth alone (5.5(c), $4 000): not met.
#ASSERT `Do my injuries reach the threshold` (LIST (`injury` "6.4(a)(i)" FALSE 0)) EQUALS `yes: the standard amounts total at least $7 500` 8000
#ASSERT `Do my injuries reach the threshold` (LIST (`injury` "5.5(c)" FALSE 0)) EQUALS `no: the standard amounts total less than $7 500, so no award for the injuries (financial loss can still be awarded)` 4000
-- Four $3 000 injuries: the three that may be awarded total 9 000, met; reg 18 gives 3 000 + 900 + 450 = 4 350.
#ASSERT `Do my injuries reach the threshold` (LIST (`injury` "1.1(a)" FALSE 0), (`injury` "2(a)" FALSE 0), (`injury` "5.4(a)" FALSE 0), (`injury` "6.3(a)" FALSE 0)) EQUALS `yes: the standard amounts total at least $7 500` 9000
#ASSERT `What is the standard amount for my injuries` (LIST (`injury` "1.1(a)" FALSE 0), (`injury` "2(a)" FALSE 0), (`injury` "5.4(a)" FALSE 0), (`injury` "6.3(a)" FALSE 0)) EQUALS `the standard amount that may be awarded for the injuries, in dollars, is` 4350
-- Finger fractures on both hands (6.3(a) doubled, $6 000) and slackened teeth (5.5(b), $3 000): 9 000, met.
#ASSERT `Do my injuries reach the threshold` (LIST (`injury` "6.3(a)" TRUE 0), (`injury` "5.5(b)" FALSE 0)) EQUALS `yes: the standard amounts total at least $7 500` 9000
-- Domestic violence injuries: $10 000, met. Non-permanent scarring alone: barred, 0, not met. An unknown item.
#ASSERT `Do my injuries reach the threshold` (LIST (`injury` "4" FALSE 0)) EQUALS `yes: the standard amounts total at least $7 500` 10000
#ASSERT `Do my injuries reach the threshold` (LIST (`scar` "13(b)" FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `no: the standard amounts total less than $7 500, so no award for the injuries (financial loss can still be awarded)` 0
#ASSERT `Do my injuries reach the threshold` (LIST (`injury` "6.7(z)" FALSE 0)) EQUALS `not covered: an item is not a leaf of Schedule 3, Part 2` "6.7(z)"

