#ASSERT `Is my application open or closed` TRUE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2026) EQUALS `open: no closure notice, or I gave updated contact details within 30 days of it (s 47H(2)(b))`
-- Notice dated 1 March 2026, no reply: closed on expiry of 30 days, 31 March 2026 (s 47J(2)); 6 months later is "31
-- September", READING the last day of September: 30 September 2026. Asked on 1 June 2026: not yet; still open to ask.
#ASSERT `Is my application open or closed` TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2026) EQUALS `closed (s 47J): I can ask the Director to reopen it until the last day given` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 9 2026)
#ASSERT `Is my application open or closed` TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 9 2026) EQUALS `closed, and the Director must reopen it: I asked within 6 months of the closure (s 47K)`
#ASSERT `Is my application open or closed` TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2026) EQUALS `closed, and it cannot be reopened: more than 6 months passed (s 47K); I may be able to make a new application`
-- Notice dated 31 July 2026: closed 30 August 2026; 6 months later "30 February 2027", READING 28 February 2027.
#ASSERT `Is my application open or closed` TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 7 2026) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2026) EQUALS `closed (s 47J): I can ask the Director to reopen it until the last day given` (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2027)

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 15. Review (s 48, Schedule 1), costs (s 54) and death (s 19). NTCAT time: HYPOTHETICAL 28 days (not deposited).
-- =====================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Can I apply for NTCAT review` `an assessor's decision under s 34 on an application for an award` TRUE 10 28 EQUALS `yes: I may apply to NTCAT for review (s 48(3)), within the NTCAT Act time I gave` 1
#ASSERT `Can I apply for NTCAT review` `an assessor's decision under s 34 on an application for an award` TRUE 40 28 EQUALS `I am the affected person (s 48(2)), but the NTCAT Act time I gave has passed` 1
#ASSERT `Can I apply for NTCAT review` `the Director's decision under s 27 on an application for an interim payment` TRUE 10 28 EQUALS `no: an interim payment decision is final and not subject to any review or appeal (s 28(1)); I can still apply for an award (s 28(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for NTCAT review` `the closure of an application under s 47J` TRUE 10 28 EQUALS `no: a closure is not a reviewable decision (Schedule 1); I can ask the Director to reopen it within 6 months (s 47K) or apply again`
-- An offender named in the application, who made a submission (s 33(3)), is not "the applicant".
#ASSERT `Can I apply for NTCAT review` `an assessor's decision under s 34 on an application for an award` FALSE 10 28 EQUALS `no: only the person named in Schedule 1 for the decision may apply (s 48(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for NTCAT review` `an assessor's decision under s 47(1) requiring a refund` TRUE 5 28 EQUALS `yes: I may apply to NTCAT for review (s 48(3)), within the NTCAT Act time I gave` 3

-- s 54: an award application, disbursements 1 200 of which counsel 500: 700. An interim payment application: s 54 does
-- not reach it (finding 12). An increased award, disbursements 300, counsel 400 (more than charged): 0.
#ASSERT `What can my lawyer charge me` `an application for an award (Division 3)` 1200 500 EQUALS `the most the legal practitioner may recover from me, in dollars, is` 700
#ASSERT `What can my lawyer charge me` `an application for an interim payment (Division 2)` 1200 500 EQUALS `s 54 does not limit the costs of an interim payment application: it covers Divisions 3, 5 and 5A only`
#ASSERT `What can my lawyer charge me` `an application for an increased award (Division 5)` 300 400 EQUALS `the most the legal practitioner may recover from me, in dollars, is` 0

#ASSERT `What happens if I die` `before applying` EQUALS `nothing passes to the estate: the eligibility does not survive (s 19(1))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I die` `after applying, before the application is decided` EQUALS `the application lapses (s 19(3)); nothing passes to the estate (s 19(1))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I die` `after the assistance is approved or awarded, before it is paid` EQUALS `the assistance is taken never to have been approved or awarded, and the application lapses (s 19(4))`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 16. Regulative rules (core). Clock: days from the approval, notice or receipt the section names.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 45: Ben's 15 900 award, notice on day 0. Paid day 20, or day 28: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 29, 45, 46(10), 47F -- the Territory must pay within 28 days` `an award (s 45)` 15900) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Territory` (`pay the amount specified in the notice` 15900) 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 29, 45, 46(10), 47F -- the Territory must pay within 28 days` `an award (s 45)` 15900) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Territory` (`pay the amount specified in the notice` 15900) 28)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the Territory, "s 45: the Territory must pay an award within 28 days ..." (paid on day 29)
#TRACE `ss 29, 45, 46(10), 47F -- the Territory must pay within 28 days` `an award (s 45)` 15900 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Territory` DOES `pay the amount specified in the notice` 15900 AT 29
-- s 29: a $5 000 interim payment, approved day 0, paid in full day 10: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 29, 45, 46(10), 47F -- the Territory must pay within 28 days` `an interim payment (s 29)` 5000) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Territory` (`pay the amount specified in the notice` 5000) 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the Territory, "s 29: ..." (only 4 000 of the 5 000 paid, nothing more by day 28)
#TRACE `ss 29, 45, 46(10), 47F -- the Territory must pay within 28 days` `an interim payment (s 29)` 5000 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Territory` DOES `pay the amount specified in the notice` 4000 AT 10
    (WAITUNTIL 29)
-- s 46(10): an increased award of 3 000 paid day 28: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 29, 45, 46(10), 47F -- the Territory must pay within 28 days` `an increased award (s 46(10))` 3000) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Territory` (`pay the amount specified in the notice` 3000) 28)) EQUALS FULFILLED

-- s 47: Ben must refund 3 000 (a later damages payment, s 47(1)(b)); the notice gives 14 days, READING 28 apply. Refund
-- on day 25 or day 28: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 47, 47G -- a person required to refund must refund within the time in the notice` `a refund of an award or interim payment (s 47)` 3000 14) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person required to refund` (`refund the amount to the Territory` 3000) 25)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 47, 47G -- a person required to refund must refund within the time in the notice` `a refund of an award or interim payment (s 47)` 3000 14) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person required to refund` (`refund the amount to the Territory` 3000) 28)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the person required to refund, "s 47(2)(c), (4): ... it is a debt owing to the Territory" (day 30)
#TRACE `ss 47, 47G -- a person required to refund must refund within the time in the notice` `a refund of an award or interim payment (s 47)` 3000 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person required to refund` DOES `refund the amount to the Territory` 3000 AT 30
-- A notice giving 60 days: refund on day 50, fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 47, 47G -- a person required to refund must refund within the time in the notice` `a refund of an award or interim payment (s 47)` 3000 60) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person required to refund` (`refund the amount to the Territory` 3000) 50)) EQUALS FULFILLED

-- s 46(1), (4): Ben, an adult paid on 15 March 2026 (day 0), may apply until 15 March 2029: 365 + 366 (February 2028)
-- + 365 = day 1096. He applies on day 1096 and the assessor decides on day 1150: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 46(1), (4) -- an increased award may be applied for within 3 years, and the assessor must decide the application` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1990)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `apply to the Director for an increased award` 1096), (EVENT `the assessor` `decide the application for an increased award` 1150)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Applying on day 1097 (16 March 2029) is too late: the right to apply has gone, no one owes anything. Fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 46(1), (4) -- an increased award may be applied for within 3 years, and the assessor must decide the application` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1990)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `apply to the Director for an increased award` 1097)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- A child paid on 1 February 2026, born 10 June 2012: until 10 June 2033. 1 February 2026 to 1 February 2033 is 5 x 365
-- + 2 x 366 (February 2028 and 2032) = 2557 days; to 10 June 2033 another 28 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 9 = 129: day 2686.
-- Applies on day 2686, decided on day 2700: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 46(1), (4) -- an increased award may be applied for within 3 years, and the assessor must decide the application` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 6 2012)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `apply to the Director for an increased award` 2686), (EVENT `the assessor` `decide the application for an increased award` 2700)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the assessor's obligation to decide the application for an increased award, still pending (s 46(4) sets no
-- period): Ben applied on day 1096, in time.
#TRACE `s 46(1), (4) -- an increased award may be applied for within 3 years, and the assessor must decide the application` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1990) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `apply to the Director for an increased award` AT 1096
    (WAITUNTIL 3000)

-- ss 47H(2)(b), 47J: a notice of proposed closure on day 0 (1 March 2026) about an award application. Updated contact
-- details on day 30 keep it to be decided; the assessor decides on day 60: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 47H(2)(b), 47J -- updated contact details within 30 days after the notice keep the application to be decided; otherwise it is closed without being decided` `an application for an award (Division 3)`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `give updated contact details to a CVSU officer` 30), (EVENT `the assessor` `decide the application` 60)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- An interim payment application: the details on day 10, the Director decides on day 20: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 47H(2)(b), 47J -- updated contact details within 30 days after the notice keep the application to be decided; otherwise it is closed without being decided` `an application for an interim payment (Division 2)`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `give updated contact details to a CVSU officer` 10), (EVENT `the Director` `decide the application` 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- No details by day 30: the application is closed without being decided (s 47J(2)); no one is in breach. The details
-- on day 31 come too late, and no one then owes a decision. Fulfilled both ways.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 47H(2)(b), 47J -- updated contact details within 30 days after the notice keep the application to be decided; otherwise it is closed without being decided` `an application for an award (Division 3)`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 31)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 47H(2)(b), 47J -- updated contact details within 30 days after the notice keep the application to be decided; otherwise it is closed without being decided` `an application for an award (Division 3)`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `give updated contact details to a CVSU officer` 31)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the assessor's obligation to decide the award application, still pending (s 34 sets no fixed period): the
-- details came on day 30, in time.
#TRACE `ss 47H(2)(b), 47J -- updated contact details within 30 days after the notice keep the application to be decided; otherwise it is closed without being decided` `an application for an award (Division 3)` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `give updated contact details to a CVSU officer` AT 30
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- s 47K, clocked from the date of the closure. A notice dated 1 March 2026 closes the application on 31 March 2026; the
-- last day to ask is 30 September 2026: 30 (April) + 31 + 30 + 31 + 31 + 30 = 183 days after the closure.
#ASSERT `the date of the closure after a notice dated` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2026
#ASSERT `the days from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2026) `to` (`the last day to ask for reopening` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2026)) EQUALS 183
-- A request on day 183 (30 September), and the Director reopens it on day 190: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 47K -- a request within 6 months of the date of the closure, and the Director must reopen the application` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2026)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `ask the Director to reopen the application` 183), (EVENT `the Director` `reopen the application` 190)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- A request on day 70 (9 June 2026) as the first event after the closure is a request in time, and the Director
-- reopens on day 80: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 47K -- a request within 6 months of the date of the closure, and the Director must reopen the application` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2026)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `ask the Director to reopen the application` 70), (EVENT `the Director` `reopen the application` 80)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- A request on day 184 (1 October 2026), or on day 251 (7 December 2026), is too late: the Director owes nothing, and
-- no one is in breach. Fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 47K -- a request within 6 months of the date of the closure, and the Director must reopen the application` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2026)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `ask the Director to reopen the application` 184)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 47K -- a request within 6 months of the date of the closure, and the Director must reopen the application` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2026)) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 100), (EVENT `the applicant` `ask the Director to reopen the application` 251)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- No request: the closure stands; no one is in breach.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 47K -- a request within 6 months of the date of the closure, and the Director must reopen the application` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2026)) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 400)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- A closure on 30 August 2026 (notice of 31 July): the last day is 28 February 2027, 1 + 30 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 31 + 28 =
-- 182 days after. A request on day 182 and reopening on day 190: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 47K -- a request within 6 months of the date of the closure, and the Director must reopen the application` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 8 2026)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `ask the Director to reopen the application` 182), (EVENT `the Director` `reopen the application` 190)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the Director's obligation to reopen the application, still pending (s 47K sets no period): the request came
-- on day 183, the last day.
#TRACE `s 47K -- a request within 6 months of the date of the closure, and the Director must reopen the application` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `ask the Director to reopen the application` AT 183
    (WAITUNTIL 1000)
